---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="The Newsletter AI Fast-Track Kit | Redefining Retirement"
  description="Pro AI prompts, exact scripts, and quick videos that get your email list live and collecting in hours, not weeks."
  type="article"
  noindex={true}
  bare={true}
>
  <article class="section">
    <div class="container narrow">

      <!-- ── HERO ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
      <header class="article-header">
        <span class="tag">The Kit &middot; $27</span>
        <h1 class="article-title">The Newsletter AI Fast-Track Kit</h1>
        <p class="article-deck">
          Pro AI prompts, exact scripts, and quick videos for every step — so your list is live and collecting <strong>in hours, not weeks</strong>, without writing a word from scratch.
        </p>
      </header>

      <!-- ── HELLO ────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
      <div class="hello-section">
        <img
          src="/images/corey-portrait.jpg"
          alt="Corey Koehler"
          class="hello-photo"
          onerror="this.style.display='none'"
        />
        <div class="hello-text">
          <h2>Hello</h2>
          <p>Hey, I'm Corey Koehler (KOH-ler).</p>
          <p>Foundry worker, then mechanical draftsman for 17 years, then midlife solopreneur.</p>
          <p>Years ago I had a blog pulling 10,000+ visitors a week from Google — and I never collected a single email. When the traffic dried up, I had nothing to show for it. The newsletter I built later, with the email list as the foundation from day one, is still paying me back today.</p>
          <p>This Kit is the shortcut version. Tick the boxes, lean on the AI prompts under each step, and you'll have your home base live in a few hours — not weeks.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- ── INTRO VIDEO WALKTHROUGH ──────────────────────────────── -->
      <div class="video-block">
        <h3 class="video-block-title">Video walkthrough</h3>
        <p class="video-block-deck">Before you start the steps below, watch this quick walkthrough of getting your home base set up.</p>
        <p class="video-block-note">Heads up: Beehiiv has updated its dashboard since I recorded this, so a few screens may look slightly different. The steps and principles are still exactly the same — just follow along for the "why," and use the written steps below for the current click-by-click.</p>
        <div class="video-embed">
          <iframe
            src="https://www.loom.com/embed/c763792cb89348d58cafbd5a9d119249"
            frameborder="0"
            webkitallowfullscreen
            mozallowfullscreen
            allowfullscreen
          ></iframe>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- ── THE HOOK ─────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
      <div class="hook-block">
        <h2>Why newsletters crush YouTube &amp; social for long-term value</h2>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>Most creators think their subscriber count equals security. Reality check:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>👉 1,000 social media followers = about $79/month</li>
            <li>👉 1,000 YouTube subs = about $79/month</li>
            <li>👉 1,000 email subs = about $582/month</li>
          </ul>
          <p>That's not my opinion — it's from a Neil Patel study of 2,501 marketers, which found email subscribers generate 7.4x more revenue per month than YouTube subscribers.</p>
          <p>And the kicker? Email subscribers don't vanish when the algorithm decides to ghost you.</p>
          <p>Email subscribers = assets you own. Average lifetime value: $37.85 each (up to $100+ in high-value niches).</p>
          <p>YouTube subs = rented attention. They only pay if they keep watching, and you're at the mercy of RPMs, ad buyers, and YouTube's mood swings.</p>
          <p>A social media follower = even more rented attention — worth just pennies ($0.01–$0.10).</p>
          <p>Translation: 10,000 social followers might bring in a couple grand if you're lucky. 10,000 email subs? That could mean a far more reliable five-figure monthly income.</p>
          <p>That's the gap. It's why smart creators are finally saying:</p>
          <p><em>"I'll use YouTube and social for discovery, but my email list is my long-term plan."</em></p>
          <p>Ok — with that out of the way, let's get your newsletter going.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- ── PROMPT SETUP (Kit Mad Libs: 5 fields, fill once) ─────── -->
      <div class="setup-block">
        <p class="setup-title">⚡ Newsletter Mad Libs: fill in the blanks once</p>
        <p class="setup-text">
          Remember Mad Libs? Same idea. Type your raw materials here once and they drop into every AI prompt on this page automatically. Paste each prompt into the <strong>same chat</strong> as you go — every step builds on the one before it, so the AI keeps your context (your niche, your gift, your name) the whole way through.
        </p>
        <div class="setup-fields">
          <div class="setup-field">
            <label class="setup-label" for="audience-input">Your ideal subscriber</label>
            <input id="audience-input" class="setup-input" type="text" placeholder="e.g., Gen X woodworkers who want to build furniture, not just watch it" autocomplete="off" />
          </div>
          <div class="setup-field">
            <label class="setup-label" for="niche-input">Your niche or topic</label>
            <input id="niche-input" class="setup-input" type="text" placeholder="e.g., fitness for 50 plus" autocomplete="off" />
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="setup-fields">
          <div class="setup-field">
            <label class="setup-label" for="platform-input">Your existing platform</label>
            <input id="platform-input" class="setup-input" type="text" placeholder="e.g., YouTube" autocomplete="off" />
          </div>
          <div class="setup-field">
            <label class="setup-label" for="audienceSize-input">Your audience size there</label>
            <input id="audienceSize-input" class="setup-input" type="text" placeholder="e.g., 4,200 subscribers" autocomplete="off" />
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="setup-field full">
          <label class="setup-label" for="existingContent-input">Your best-performing posts, videos, or one-liners</label>
          <input id="existingContent-input" class="setup-input" type="text" placeholder="e.g., the '5 tools every beginner needs' video" autocomplete="off" />
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- ── PROGRESS ─────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
      <div class="progress-wrap">
        <div class="progress-label">
          <span>Your progress</span>
          <span id="progress-count">0 / 0 done</span>
        </div>
        <div class="progress-track">
          <div class="progress-fill" id="progress-fill"></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- ── STEPS ────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
      <div class="steps">

        <!-- STEP 1 -->
        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-num">Step 1</div>
          <div class="step-content">
            <h2 class="step-title">Pick something worth trading an email for</h2>
            <div class="prose">
              <p>A "gift" is just something useful enough that a stranger hands over their email address for it. It doesn't need to be complicated, and it definitely doesn't need to take you a week to make.</p>
              <p>When I did this, I started with stuff I'd already made — a post that did well, an answer to the question people kept asking me. The work was already done. I just packaged it up.</p>
              <p>Don't overthink it. Pick from:</p>
              <ul>
                <li>A "how-to" post or video that already performed well</li>
                <li>An answer to the question you get asked all the time</li>
                <li>Or just open a waitlist and figure out the gift later — that's allowed</li>
              </ul>
              <p>If you're starting from nothing, here's a shortlist of fast ideas:</p>
              <ul>
                <li>Checklist</li>
                <li>Quick guide or cheat sheet</li>
                <li>A list of tools, sites, or books you actually use</li>
                <li>A short case study or mini workbook</li>
                <li>Something exclusive — a video, article, or podcast episode</li>
                <li>A mini course or quiz</li>
                <li>A template</li>
              </ul>
              <p>You don't need to build the gift today. Just decide what it is — you'll need it for Step 2.</p>
            </div>
            <ul class="checklist">
              <li><label class="check-item"><input type="checkbox" data-id="s1-1"><span>Pick something worth trading an email for — a checklist, short guide, template, tool list, or mini case study.</span></label></li>
              <li><label class="check-item"><input type="checkbox" data-id="s1-2"><span>Don't build from scratch if you don't have to — repackage something that already worked (a post, a video, an answer you give people all the time).</span></label></li>
              <li><label class="check-item"><input type="checkbox" data-id="s1-3"><span>Decide what it is now. You'll attach it in Step 4.</span></label></li>
            </ul>
            <div class="prompt-block">
              <div class="ap-head">
                <p class="prompt-label">🔒 Pro prompt — paste this into ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini, or your favorite LLM, and keep using this same chat for every prompt on this page:</p>
                <button type="button" class="copy-btn" data-copy>Copy</button>
              </div>
              <pre>You are a lead-generation strategist helping me pick a lead magnet for a brand-new newsletter about <span class="ph" data-ph="niche">[your niche]</span>. My ideal subscriber is <span class="ph" data-ph="audience">[your ideal subscriber]</span>. I already have an audience on <span class="ph" data-ph="platform">[your platform]</span> (<span class="ph" data-ph="audienceSize">[audience size]</span>), and here's what's already worked for me: <span class="ph" data-ph="existingContent">[your best content]</span>.

Walk me through it step by step:

Step 1: Start from what I've already made — ask me which piece above got the strongest reaction, and what question my audience asks me all the time.

Step 2: Ask me whether I'd rather repackage something that exists or build something new.

Step 3: Based on my answers, give me 5 lead magnet ideas I could realistically finish in one afternoon — pulled from what I've already made wherever possible. For each: the format, the promise or headline, and why my <span class="ph" data-ph="platform">[your platform]</span> audience would trade their email for it.

Step 4: Ask me which one I'm picking, then write a single clear sentence describing it — I'll reuse that sentence when I name my newsletter and write my welcome email later.

Keep it plain-spoken. No hype, no buzzwords.</pre>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- STEP 2 -->
        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-num">Step 2</div>
          <div class="step-content">
            <h2 class="step-title">Set up your home base on Beehiiv</h2>
            <div class="prose">
              <p>I use Beehiiv, and it's what I'd pick again starting today — solid analytics, a built-in referral system, and a free plan up to 2,500 subscribers.</p>
            </div>
            <ul class="checklist">
              <li><label class="check-item"><input type="checkbox" data-id="s2-1"><span>Sign up for Beehiiv (the free plan is plenty to start).</span></label></li>
              <li><label class="check-item"><input type="checkbox" data-id="s2-2"><span>Fill in Settings &rarr; General Info — basics only, don't overthink it.</span></label></li>
              <li><label class="check-item"><input type="checkbox" data-id="s2-3"><span>Skip the advanced settings for now. You can come back to those later.</span></label></li>
            </ul>

            <div class="inline-cta">
              <p>If you sign up through my link and use the code <strong class="coupon">QUICKSTART</strong> at checkout, you get 20% off your first three months.</p>
              <a
                href="https://www.beehiiv.com?via=QUICKSTART"
                class="btn"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
              >
                Start free on Beehiiv &rarr;
              </a>
              <p class="cta-note">Free plan available. Affiliate link — I earn a small commission at no cost to you.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="prose">
              <p>Once you're signed up, go to Settings &rarr; General Info and fill in your details. This part's just data entry.</p>
            </div>

            <figure class="screenshot-slot">
              <img
                src="/images/beehiiv-create.png"
                alt="Beehiiv's create a new publication screen"
                loading="lazy"
                onerror="this.closest('figure').style.display='none'"
              />
              <figcaption>Beehiiv's "create a new publication" screen.</figcaption>
            </figure>

            <div class="prose">
              <p>A few other basics while you're in there:</p>
              <ul>
                <li>Add a logo and thumbnail. Canva works fine if you don't have one — or take the size Beehiiv asks for on that screen and ask Gemini, ChatGPT, or any AI image tool to generate one for you.</li>
                <li>Pick 3 publication tags.</li>
                <li>Set your language and time zone.</li>
              </ul>
              <p>Leave everything else for later — we're keeping this simple.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="prompt-block">
              <div class="ap-head">
                <p class="prompt-label">🔒 Pro prompt — paste this into ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini, or your favorite LLM. One tip: for a how-to question like this, Perplexity tends to do well — it's current and pulls in tutorials and video walkthroughs, not just text.</p>
                <button type="button" class="copy-btn" data-copy>Copy</button>
              </div>
              <pre>You are a Beehiiv setup consultant. I'm creating a new publication for a newsletter about <span class="ph" data-ph="niche">[your niche]</span>, written for <span class="ph" data-ph="audience">[your ideal subscriber]</span>.

Walk me through it step by step:

Step 1: Tell me exactly which settings under Settings &rarr; General Info actually matter when I'm just starting — sender name, reply-to address, time zone, publication tags — and why each one matters for deliverability or growth.

Step 2: Tell me which advanced settings (custom domains, integrations, advanced automations) I can safely ignore until I have subscribers, so I don't waste time on them now.

Step 3: I already picked a lead magnet in Step 1 of this Kit — based on that, write me a two-sentence publication description and suggest 3 publication tags that fit my niche and audience.

Give me a short checklist I can run through in under 10 minutes.</pre>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- STEP 3 -->
        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-num">Step 3</div>
          <div class="step-content">
            <h2 class="step-title">Name it + write your two-line pitch</h2>
            <div class="prose">
              <p>The rule: clear beats clever, every time.</p>
              <p><strong>Avoid:</strong> something vague like "Marketing Musings."</p>
              <p><strong>Try:</strong> something that tells people exactly what's inside — "[Outcome] for [Audience]."</p>
              <p>Then write your two-line pitch. This is the bit people skip, and shouldn't:</p>
              <ul>
                <li><strong>Line 1 (the hook):</strong> Who it's for + the problem + the outcome</li>
                <li><strong>Line 2 (the lever):</strong> A call to action + the benefit</li>
              </ul>
              <p><em>Example: "Helping parents exhausted by screen-time battles set boundaries that actually stick. Enter your email and join the waitlist to get 5 quick scripts that make unplugging easier."</em></p>
            </div>
            <ul class="checklist">
              <li><label class="check-item"><input type="checkbox" data-id="s3-1"><span>Pick a name where clear beats clever — "Outcome for Audience" beats "Marketing Musings" every time.</span></label></li>
              <li><label class="check-item"><input type="checkbox" data-id="s3-2"><span>Write your two-line pitch — Line 1 is the hook (who it's for + problem + outcome), Line 2 is the lever (a call to action + benefit).</span></label></li>
            </ul>

            <figure class="screenshot-slot">
              <img
                src="/images/beehiiv-details.png"
                alt="Beehiiv publication details settings"
                loading="lazy"
                onerror="this.closest('figure').style.display='none'"
              />
              <figcaption>Settings &rarr; Publication Details.</figcaption>
            </figure>

            <div class="prompt-block">
              <div class="ap-head">
                <p class="prompt-label">🔒 Pro prompt — paste this into ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini, or your favorite LLM:</p>
                <button type="button" class="copy-btn" data-copy>Copy</button>
              </div>
              <pre>You are a newsletter growth expert. I want you to help me name my newsletter and create a 2-line waitlist pitch. It's about <span class="ph" data-ph="niche">[your niche]</span> for <span class="ph" data-ph="audience">[your ideal subscriber]</span>, and I'm bringing an existing audience from <span class="ph" data-ph="platform">[your platform]</span> (<span class="ph" data-ph="audienceSize">[audience size]</span>).

Walk me through it step by step.

Step 1: Ask me what I want my readers to do (not "learn") and help me phrase it in action terms.

Step 2: Ask me to niche it down. Help me pick the slice of my <span class="ph" data-ph="platform">[your platform]</span> audience most likely to subscribe first.

Step 3: Ask me to pick 1 problem my audience has and 1 outcome they want. Combine into a single clear sentence.

Step 4: Help me add a call-to-action line that starts with "Enter your email and join the waitlist to get…" and ends with a concrete benefit.

Then give me 10 name options where clear beats clever — "[Outcome] for [Audience]" beats cute wordplay — and 3 variations of my 2-line waitlist pitch in plain, conversational language.</pre>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- STEP 4 -->
        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-num">Step 4</div>
          <div class="step-content">
            <h2 class="step-title">Build your signup page &amp; attach the gift</h2>
            <ul class="checklist">
              <li><label class="check-item"><input type="checkbox" data-id="s4-1"><span>Use Beehiiv's built-in page builder — you don't need a separate website.</span></label></li>
              <li><label class="check-item"><input type="checkbox" data-id="s4-2"><span>Write one headline, one subheadline, one call to action.</span></label></li>
              <li><label class="check-item"><input type="checkbox" data-id="s4-3"><span>Attach the gift from Step 1 so it delivers automatically.</span></label></li>
            </ul>

            <figure class="screenshot-slot">
              <img
                src="/images/beehiiv-landing.png"
                alt="Beehiiv landing page and subscribe form builder"
                loading="lazy"
                onerror="this.closest('figure').style.display='none'"
              />
              <figcaption>Website &rarr; landing page / subscribe form builder.</figcaption>
            </figure>

            <div class="prompt-block">
              <div class="ap-head">
                <p class="prompt-label">🔒 Pro prompt — paste this into ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini, or your favorite LLM:</p>
                <button type="button" class="copy-btn" data-copy>Copy</button>
              </div>
              <pre>You are a direct-response copywriter. I'm building the signup page for my newsletter about <span class="ph" data-ph="niche">[your niche]</span>, aimed at <span class="ph" data-ph="audience">[your ideal subscriber]</span>.

I've already got a free gift, a newsletter name, and a two-line pitch from the steps above.

Walk me through it step by step:

Step 1: Ask me to paste my newsletter name and two-line pitch from Step 3.

Step 2: Ask me what the free gift is and what format it's in (checklist, guide, template, etc.) from Step 1.

Step 3: Using my answers, write a headline under 10 words, a subheadline, 3 benefit bullets, and one clear call to action that mentions the gift by name — written to convert a <span class="ph" data-ph="platform">[your platform]</span> follower who's never clicked away from the feed for me before.

Step 4: Give me 2 alternate headlines in case the first one doesn't land.

Keep it plain-spoken — no hype, no hard sell.</pre>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- STEP 5 -->
        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-num">Step 5</div>
          <div class="step-content">
            <h2 class="step-title">Write your welcome email</h2>
            <ul class="checklist">
              <li><label class="check-item"><input type="checkbox" data-id="s5-1"><span>Say who you are, what they'll get, and how often.</span></label></li>
              <li><label class="check-item"><input type="checkbox" data-id="s5-2"><span>Deliver the gift right away — no waiting.</span></label></li>
              <li><label class="check-item"><input type="checkbox" data-id="s5-3"><span>Ask them to reply with one question. It boosts deliverability and starts a real conversation.</span></label></li>
            </ul>

            <figure class="screenshot-slot">
              <img
                src="/images/beehiiv-welcome.png"
                alt="Beehiiv automations welcome email editor"
                loading="lazy"
                onerror="this.closest('figure').style.display='none'"
              />
              <figcaption>Automations &rarr; welcome email editor.</figcaption>
            </figure>

            <div class="prose">
              <p><strong>Example:</strong></p>
              <div class="script">
                <button type="button" class="copy-btn" data-copy>Copy</button>
                <blockquote>
                  <p><strong>Subject:</strong> Here's your [gift name] (+ a quick favor)</p>
                  <p>Hey [First Name],</p>
                  <p>Thanks for signing up. Here's your [gift name] &rarr; [link]</p>
                  <p>I'm Corey — I send <span class="ph" data-ph="niche">[your niche]</span> tips like this every [day of week]. No fluff, just what's worked for me.</p>
                  <p>Quick favor: hit reply and tell me the one thing you're stuck on right now. I read every reply, and it helps me write issues that actually help.</p>
                  <p>Talk soon,<br>Corey</p>
                </blockquote>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="prompt-block">
              <div class="ap-head">
                <p class="prompt-label">🔒 Pro prompt — paste this into ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini, or your favorite LLM:</p>
                <button type="button" class="copy-btn" data-copy>Copy</button>
              </div>
              <pre>You are an email copywriter. I'm writing the welcome email for my newsletter about <span class="ph" data-ph="niche">[your niche]</span>, for <span class="ph" data-ph="audience">[your ideal subscriber]</span>.

I've already got a free gift, a newsletter name, and a two-line pitch from the steps above.

Walk me through it step by step:

Step 1: Ask me to paste the gift, the name, and the pitch from the earlier steps.

Step 2: Ask me how often I plan to send (weekly, biweekly) and what day.

Step 3: Using my answers, write a warm welcome email under 200 words that says who I am, sets expectations for what they'll get and how often, delivers the gift right away, and asks them to reply with one specific question.

Step 4: Give me one alternate subject line option.

Keep it conversational — like a real person, not a marketing team.</pre>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>

      <!-- ── MILESTONE: HOME BASE DONE ─────────────────────────────── -->
      <div class="milestone-block">
        <p>🎉 <strong>Your home base is live.</strong> That's the deliverable — a newsletter you actually own. Everything from here is about getting a few people onto it.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- ── BONUS: FIRST SUBSCRIBERS (QUICK WIN) ─────────────────── -->
      <div class="bonus-block">
        <p class="result-section-label">Bonus</p>
        <h2>Get your first subscribers (the quick win)</h2>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>Your list is live. Here's how to get a few people on it this week — no audience required.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="video-embed">
          <iframe
            src="https://www.loom.com/embed/7c909354370d435b91b0019f7cf815fe"
            frameborder="0"
            webkitallowfullscreen
            mozallowfullscreen
            allowfullscreen
          ></iframe>
        </div>

        <div class="script-setup">
          <p class="setup-title">⚡ One more round of Mad Libs</p>
          <p class="setup-text">Drop in your topic and signup link — they'll fill into every script below. Hit <strong>Copy</strong>, then personalize the [First Name] bits as you send.</p>
          <div class="setup-fields">
            <div class="setup-field">
              <label class="setup-label" for="topic-input">Your newsletter topic</label>
              <input id="topic-input" class="setup-input" type="text" placeholder="e.g., personal finance for creators" autocomplete="off" />
            </div>
            <div class="setup-field">
              <label class="setup-label" for="link-input">Your signup link</label>
              <input id="link-input" class="setup-input" type="text" placeholder="e.g., yourname.beehiiv.com" autocomplete="off" />
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="prose">
          <h3>1. Reach out directly</h3>
          <p>Message people you actually know. Not a mass blast — a real message, one at a time.</p>
          <div class="script">
            <button type="button" class="copy-btn" data-copy>Copy</button>
            <blockquote>
              <p><strong>Subject:</strong> Quick question, [First Name]</p>
              <p>Hey [First Name],</p>
              <p>I'm starting a newsletter about <span class="ph" data-ph="topic">[TOPIC]</span>, and I'd love to include you.</p>
              <p>Want in? Just reply and let me know.</p>
            </blockquote>
          </div>
          <p>When they say yes:</p>
          <div class="script">
            <button type="button" class="copy-btn" data-copy>Copy</button>
            <blockquote>
              <p>Awesome! Just click this link to sign up: <span class="ph" data-ph="link">[link]</span></p>
              <p>Or drop me your best email, and I'll add you myself.</p>
            </blockquote>
          </div>
          <p>After they sign up:</p>
          <div class="script">
            <button type="button" class="copy-btn" data-copy>Copy</button>
            <blockquote>
              <p>Thank you! By the way, do you know one other person who'd be interested too?</p>
            </blockquote>
          </div>

          <h3>2. DM your social connections (one by one)</h3>
          <p>Go through your friends, followers, and connections on LinkedIn, Facebook, Instagram, TikTok — wherever you're already active.</p>
          <p><strong>Message 1:</strong></p>
          <div class="script">
            <button type="button" class="copy-btn" data-copy>Copy</button>
            <blockquote><p>Hey [First Name]!</p></blockquote>
          </div>
          <p><strong>Message 2</strong> (when they respond):</p>
          <div class="script">
            <button type="button" class="copy-btn" data-copy>Copy</button>
